PolyStrata - Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, GLM 5.3 Flash and smaller MoE models on a normal PC (a GPU + system RAM + CPU)

=== Step 1: checking your PC ===
  Your AMD GPUs:
    GPU 0: AMD Radeon 8060S (Ryzen AI Max, Strix Halo, gfx1151), unified memory: 1.0 GB BIOS carve-out + 118 GB shared with the RAM, 119 GB usable by the GPU - can be used
  [ok] GPU: AMD Radeon 8060S (Ryzen AI Max, Strix Halo, gfx1151), unified memory: 1.0 GB BIOS carve-out + 118 GB shared with the RAM, 119 GB usable by the GPU, gfx1151 (AMD: docs/STRIX_HALO.md)
  Strix Halo (gfx1151, Ryzen AI Max): the CPU and the GPU share one memory pool (124 GB seen by the OS + a 1.0 GB BIOS carve-out), so the model's experts live in that pool and the expert cache is sized from the memory the OS can give back, not from the carve-out.
  The engine is compiled here for gfx1151 (experimental, measured on one machine): see docs/STRIX_HALO.md.
  Recommended model: UD-IQ4_XS (the one docs/STRIX_HALO.md measures); the menus list the others.
  [ok] RAM: 124 GB
  [ok] CPU: AMD RYZEN AI MAX+ 395 w/ Radeon 8060S (AVX-512)

=== Step 2: your choices ===
  [ok] model: Gemma 4 26B-A4B
  Images: the image encoder is a CUDA program: on the AMD card images are off (text answers).

  UD-Q4_K_M: 4- and 5-bit experts (Unsloth Dynamic); the same draft model; download 17 GB. The file is read in place: about 14 of
  its 14 GB of experts fit this card, the rest stay in RAM (the OS file cache).
  [ok] size: UD-Q4_K_M
  [ok] context: 32768 tokens

  Conversation cache: a coding agent sends several conversations in turn (the main one, its subagents,
  short side requests). With the cache, one that makes room for another is kept in RAM and comes back
  without being read again. It takes what it holds, up to 8 GB of RAM, and
  less when little RAM is left free once the model is loaded.
  [ok] conversation cache: 40% of the RAM free once the model is loaded, up to 8192 MiB

=== Step 3: Python packages ===
  [ok] numpy, jinja2, regex, pyyaml, tqdm, requests, cmake, ninja, pillow, psutil already installed

